==============================================================================
[6] VERDICT
==============================================================================
 [T] phi^U expands into spanning trees (Penrose), signs +-; block product (1.3) is exact.
 [T] tau route cannot reach 3.5: sup tau^{1/n} >= 16.361  (periodic 4D box, exact).
 [T] the <=20 loss: e*Delta (positions) is charged twice; residual = shape entropy <= e.
 [C] e (2.7183) and Otter (2.9558) both < 3.5 -> Cbar <= 3.5 provable at the level of ubar.
 [E] per-cluster sup observed: (n-1)!^{1/n} to n=6, max 120^{1/6}=2.2209 (exact, clique<=6).
     Chat=2 exact   : Chat*Cbar = 5.4365637 < 7.0632853 ; beta1^fix = 0.027067057 = 1.299219 x (1/48) >= 1/48 (NO shrink)
     Chat=4 envelope: Chat*Cbar = 10.873127 > 7.0632853 ; beta1^fix = 0.013533528 = 0.6496094 x (1/48) < 1/48 (shrinks)
 => (a) TRIGGERS with Chat=2: Cbar <= e <= 3.5, Chat*Cbar = 5.4366 < 7.0633,
    beta1^fix = 1.2992*(1/48) >= 1/48 -> window back to 1/48, no shrink.
    (with the stronger c01 tree identity Cbar=1: 2*1=2 < 7.0633, beta1 = 3.53*(1/48).)
 => (b) does NOT trigger for Cbar itself (provable lower bound 2.2209 < 3.5); it DOES
    trigger for the tau-envelope (>= 16.36), which is therefore abandoned as an object.
 => (c) the '<=20' error is bookkeeping (position entropy twice), not the AM-GM algebra.
    NB a01's 'non-vacuity check' (planar grids 2.05-2.37) understates real 4D clusters:
    the genuine L=2 box already sits at 16.36, i.e. the Delta=20 envelope is nearly SATURATED.

